# Living Survey: brain                                                                                         
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Introduction                                                                                                
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **brain**.                                          
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Neuro-Oncology and Therapeutic Innovations                                                                  
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
Recent advances in brain tumor segmentation and diagnosis have leveraged advanced deep learning architectures. 
NeuroTS-Net [^2609.16873] and DE-GAN [^2609.16755] introduce novel 3D CNN and conditional GAN frameworks that  
significantly improve multi-class semantic segmentation of pediatric brain tumors and enhance tumor-core       
delineation in FLAIR images. Complementing these, BrainVLM [^2609.16597] integrates vision-language modeling   
with uncertainty quantification to classify WHO brain tumor types and generate radiology reports, while GRIN+  
[^2609.15571] addresses machine unlearning for imbalanced medical data to preserve privacy without sacrificing 
diagnostic accuracy. Generalization across heterogeneous populations is further evaluated in BraTS-GoAT 2026   
[^2609.15524], highlighting the challenges of small enhancing tumor volumes. Therapeutic delivery mechanisms   
are also advancing, with lipid nanoparticle formulations targeting TERT [^10.17030_uclan.thesis.00059253] and  
[^10.17030_uclan.thesis.00059033] showing promise in overcoming the blood-brain barrier for glioblastoma.      
Furthermore, liquid biopsy approaches utilizing cell-free DNA nucleosome positioning [^10.5526_err-00042862]   
and [^10.5526_err-00042900] offer non-invasive diagnostic potential, while single-cell spatial atlases         
[^10.5281_zenodo.21816284], [^10.5281_zenodo.21816285], [^10.5281_zenodo.21782885], [^10.5281_zenodo.21782884] 
map pan-cancer metastatic brain tumors. Secretome and extracellular vesicle modulation from neural crest stem  
cells [^10.48683_1926.00128572] and RET signaling pathways in breast cancer brain metastasis                   
[^10.5281_zenodo.19501083], [^10.5281_zenodo.19501082] provide new avenues for understanding tumor             
microenvironments and metastatic mechanisms.                                                                   
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Neuroimaging and Signal Processing                                                                          
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
The analysis of brain signals and imaging modalities continues to evolve with robust benchmarks and foundation 
models. iMINDBench [^2609.18104] establishes a standardized framework for iEEG neural decoding across          
institutions, revealing the limits of scaling supervised data. For broader brain signal analysis, METIS        
[^2609.15740] introduces a language-guided multimodal foundation model pretrained on over 70,000 hours of      
recordings, achieving state-of-the-art zero-shot performance. Medical image synthesis and uncertainty          
quantification are addressed by MUMINS [^2609.17169], which jointly diffuses baseline scans and follow-up      
residuals to predict anatomical changes. Diffusion MRI synthesis is improved via DTI-SHNet [^2609.14312], which
performs spatially aware volumetric regression to generate multi-shell data from single-shell inputs. Cerebral 
hemodynamics are visualized in real-time using a 4D microvascular imaging platform for stroke models           
[^2609.16666], while TractSpLearn [^2609.15342] detects subtle white matter alterations in traumatic brain     
injury through shared-manifold learning. Schizophrenia detection benefits from transformer-based EEG           
spectrogram analysis [^2609.14015], and 3D object reconstruction from brain signals is advanced by Mind2Cloud  
[^2609.13991], which employs two-granularity diffusion decoding. Dynamic functional connectivity is further    
explored using a novel nonparametric correlation estimator [^2609.13848]. Cognitive and structural brain       
changes are linked to age and culture in studies examining gray matter volumes [^10.48617_etd.1671], while     
infant temperament is correlated with EEG microstates [^10.7273_000007929]. Cross-organ metabolic profiling    
also highlights specific brain uptake and release patterns [^10.5281_zenodo.20652506],                         
[^10.5281_zenodo.20652505].                                                                                    
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Computational Neuroscience and Brain Modeling                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
Theoretical and computational models are providing deeper insights into brain dynamics, digital twins, and     
evolutionary adaptations. Transcranial holography for deep-brain stimulation is optimized through phase        
unwrapping techniques [^2609.18495], while moderate neural noise is shown to enable accurate internal          
simulation of rare events in Bayesian networks [^2609.18033]. Graphlet-based structural fingerprints           
[^2609.17445] outperform classical measures in analyzing resting-state connectomes. Hippocampus-inspired       
spiking neural networks are successfully mapped to neuromorphic memristive hardware [^2609.16429], and         
dichoptic foveation models [^2609.16385] explain interocular visual perception in VR. Evolutionary neurobiology
suggests that large brains may evolve in stable environments before colonizing dynamic ones [^2609.15569].     
Disease progression modeling is inverted to reconstruct healthier brain states from diseased MRIs in           
Alzheimer's research [^2609.14590]. Neurosurgical training is enhanced by ex-vivo calf brain models with       
integrated force sensors [^2609.14198]. Faithful stochastic models for brain digital twins [^2609.13973]       
propose new computational frameworks, while brain-based digital twins for motor imagery                        
[^10.17870_bathspa.00017805] integrate EEG and kinematics for real-time feedback. At the molecular level,      
circRNAs serve as biomarkers for biological aging in the brain [^10.48617_etd.1568], and spatial codes         
governing olfactory receptor choice align sensory maps in the nose and brain [^10.5281_zenodo.18941307],       
[^10.5281_zenodo.18941308]. Central vagal afferent signaling in the nucleus of the solitary tract              
[^10.7273_000008411] and nitric oxide signaling in Parkinson's disease [^10.4103_mgr.medgasres-d-26-00008]     
further elucidate neurochemical pathways. The amyloid precursor protein is re-evaluated as a universal survival
molecule rather than solely a pathological target in Alzheimer's [^10.5281_zenodo.20049820].                   
                                                                                                               

